::CW_U01_PRE_Q01::[MLA.CW.COM.02] The draft line is: "The hallway swallowed the final bell." Question: Which response best demonstrates workshop feedback?
{
~A. This response changes the meaning of the passage.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
=B. clear feedback should name a craft choice and reader effect.#Correct. This names the craft choice and explains the effect and stays aligned to Creative Writing craft work.
~C. This response judges the writer instead of the writing.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
~D. This response ignores the craft choice named in the question.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
}

::CW_U01_PRE_Q02::[MLA.CW.COM.03] The line is: "Obviously, my locker chose today to become a cave." Question: Which response best demonstrates voice and tone?
{
~A. This response gives only a vague opinion without evidence.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
~B. This response judges the writer instead of the writing.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
~C. This response ignores the craft choice named in the question.#Incorrect. This does not provide clear, standards-aligned craft reasoning.
=D. the voice is sarcastic and exaggerated.#Correct. This identifies sarcastic voice from diction and stays aligned to Creative Writing craft work.
}

::CW_U01_PRE_Q03::[MLA.CW.COM.04] The sentence is: "The candle trembled in the window." Question: Which response best demonstrates craft vocabulary?
{
